<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">New Phocaea</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Yeni Foça</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phocaea">Phocaea</a>, today Yeni Foça in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, was a fortified town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> coast founded by the Genoese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaccaria">Zaccaria family</a> in the late 13th century to protect the nearby alum mines. Alum made it one of the most valuable Genoese possessions in the east. It passed to the Genoese maona of Chios in 1346 and fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in 1455.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/new-phocaea.jpg" alt="New Phocaea" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mr. Vehbi Moğol · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yenifocageneral.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
